 **[Cache expensive Mathematical Look-Up Tables]**
 **Learning:** In algorithms like posterization, computing `((val / 255.0 * factor).round() / factor * 255.0) as u32` inside a per-pixel loop is a major bottleneck due to floating-point divisions and `.round()` calls. Precalculating a 256-element Look-Up Table (LUT) maps the 8-bit channel (0..=255) to its posterized value in O(1) time without thread-locals.
